       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a hepatotoxic dose, and I know of no indication that would justify it for a 70 kg adult. A single 5 g dose could already be in the range that needs acetylcysteine monitoring. If I entered it, the patient could be seriously harmed before anyone caught it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 650 mg PO four times daily. I can add a note with the indication and a max daily dose.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy.** If you're working from a protocol or a specific reason for the higher dose, a pharmacist or toxicology can review it first.\n- **Check for a different intent.** If you meant a different drug or a different unit, tell me and I'll re-check the order.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
